    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/48924181-9ab488d9-e6fe-4a24-9db4-849907b27896?source=collection_link",
    "description": "Seed and demo requests for product-service, sent through the API gateway (gatewayUrl, port 8086).\n\nCreate, update and delete need an ADMIN token. A collection-level pre-request script logs in as the dev admin user at Keycloak (keycloakUrl, port 8180) whenever it has no token or the 5-minute token is about to expire, so every request works on its own. Dev credentials only (see keycloak/realm-export.json). Start the stack first (`docker compose up` in parent/).\n\nRun the requests in order. The three creates add products and remember their ids (shoesProductId, topsProductId, bottomsProductId); the delete and update then use those ids, so it works on a database with any existing data. Each run adds three products and deletes one of them."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Create product (shoes)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n    \"category\": \"shoes\",\n    \"image\": \"nullURL\",\n    \"price\": \"150.25\",\n    \"status\": \"True\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": "{{productUrl}}"
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Created (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const product = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('shoesProductId', String(product.pid));",
              "pm.test('Response has a product id', () => pm.expect(product.pid).to.be.a('number'));"
            ]
